# Email scripts (SharePoint library), countries & languages, agents and branding.
# Library layout: Scripts/{Air|Ocean|General}/<script name>/<language>.docx (+ .pdf),
# Banners/{Air|Ocean}/<CC or country name|default>.png, Brand/logo.png, Brand/badge-*.png.
# Until SharePoint is configured the library is a local folder (LOCAL_DOCUMENTS_PATH).
# The upload examples read ./samples/tr.docx and ./samples/TR.png: put your own files there.
# The CSV office column is matched by office name.

@token = PASTE-AN-ADMIN-DEV-TOKEN
@templateId = PASTE-A-SCRIPT-TEMPLATE-ID
@senderId = PASTE-AN-AGENT-ID
@scriptKey = air_usa_canada_air_to_country

### Script × language matrix (18 languages from the countries table)
GET {{baseUrl}}/scripts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One script version (HTML, import warnings, SharePoint links)
GET {{baseUrl}}/scripts/templates/{{templateId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Exact preview for a destination country (and optionally an agent or a real contact)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/templates/{{templateId}}/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "TR",
  "sender_id": "{{senderId}}"
}

### Upload a Word script: saved into the library, then imported (PDF = reference copy)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: upload-air-intro-tr-001
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LaneReach

--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="script_name"

USA-Canada air to country
--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="service_line"

air
--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="language"

tr
--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="tr.docx"
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document

< ./samples/tr.docx
--LaneReach--

### Start a script from text (a Word file is generated in the library)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/blank
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: blank-ocean-intro-001

{
  "script_name": "Ocean intro",
  "service_line": "ocean",
  "language": "en",
  "subject": "Ocean freight {to_country}",
  "body": "Hi {first_name|there},\n\nAny ocean enquiries from the USA or Canada {to_country}?\n\n{banner}\n\nBest regards,\n\n{signature}\n\nYou're receiving this email as a fellow {network} member.\n\n{unsubscribe_link|Unsubscribe here}"
}

### Sync the library now (also runs every 5 minutes)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: sync-now-001

### AI-translate missing languages (saved as AI drafts; not sent until approved)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/{{scriptKey}}/translate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: translate-air-001

{
  "languages": ["fr", "es"]
}

### Approve an AI draft (needs workflows:publish)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/templates/{{templateId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: approve-draft-001

### Upload a country banner (omit country for the default banner)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/banners
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: banner-air-tr-001
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LaneReach

--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="service_line"

air
--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="country"

TR
--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="TR.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./samples/TR.png
--LaneReach--

### Images in the library (banners, logos, badges)
GET {{baseUrl}}/scripts/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Countries & languages
GET {{baseUrl}}/countries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add or change a country (language = script variant, phrase in that language)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/countries/BR
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Brazil",
  "language": "pt-br",
  "to_country_phrase": "para o Brasil",
  "allow_language_fallback": true,
  "is_enabled": true
}

### Agents: import the 24 agents (CSV columns: name,email,office,service_line,title,phone,daily_cap)
POST {{baseUrl}}/senders/import
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: agents-import-001
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LaneReach

--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="agents.csv"
Content-Type: text/csv

name,email,office,service_line,title,phone,daily_cap
Molly Example,molly@forwarder.example,USA/Canada,air,Marketing Executive,+1 905-000-0000,50
--LaneReach--

### An agent's signature (HTML + text)
GET {{baseUrl}}/senders/{{senderId}}/signature
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Branding used by generated signatures
GET {{baseUrl}}/settings/branding
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Library connection (local folder or SharePoint; the secret comes from SHAREPOINT_CLIENT_SECRETS)
GET {{baseUrl}}/settings/library
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
PUT {{baseUrl}}/settings/library
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "provider": "sharepoint",
  "site_url": "https://contoso.sharepoint.com/sites/Marketing",
  "library_name": "Documents",
  "root_folder": "LaneReach",
  "azure_tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "client_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### Test the connection
POST {{baseUrl}}/settings/library/test
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Brand images for generated signatures: kind = logo | qr | promo | badge (saved to Brand/)
POST {{baseUrl}}/scripts/brand-images
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: brand-qr-001
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=LaneReach

--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="kind"

qr
--LaneReach
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="qr.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./samples/qr.png
--LaneReach--
